{"message":"Your clearest starting point is your **leg motion**: in this free throw, you bend your knee and straighten it as you rise toward release. That’s a useful part of the motion to keep if it feels comfortable; this clip alone doesn’t show that you need a deeper or shallower dip.

I wouldn’t prescribe a form change yet. The elbow measurements aren’t reliable enough to judge your arm, and the recorded miss comes from an experimental detector rather than a confirmed result. One attempt also can’t tell us what you repeat.

**Next step:** Record a small set of free throws from the same steady angle, with your whole body in view. Check whether your dip and rise feel comfortable and look similar across attempts, and record the results yourself. That will give us a better basis for choosing what to improve.","evidence_ids":["shot:free_throw_01_shot_1","shot:free_throw_01_shot_1:knee_angle_range"],"frame_ids":["frame:free_throw_01_shot_1:knee_dip:38:knee:","frame:free_throw_01_shot_1:knee_extension:49:knee:knee_dip"],"visual":"knee_straightens"}

